{"id":"n72e377a04d","headline":"Rand and JSE firm as markets cheer Middle East ceasefire","summary":"The rand and the JSE firmed as markets welcomed the Middle East ceasefire. The oil price and the dollar fell on hopes that oil will flow through the Strait of Hormuz.","why":"The rand is South Africa's currency, and the JSE is the country's main stock exchange. Both are sensitive to oil prices and global risk appetite.","category":"markets","event_type":"geopolitics","importance":2,"flag":null,"market_moving":true,"location":{"place":"Johannesburg","country":"South Africa","lat":-26.204,"lon":28.047,"region":"af"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"Business Day","url":"https://www.businessday.co.za/markets/2026-04-08-rand-and-jse-firm-as-markets-cheer-middle-east-ceasefire/"},"sources":[{"name":"Business Day","url":"https://www.businessday.co.za/markets/2026-04-08-rand-and-jse-firm-as-markets-cheer-middle-east-ceasefire/"}],"published_at":"2026-04-08T07:34:03Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-17T17:30:28Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"d1eefb3ffe1177ef","impacts":[],"why_moved":"The ceasefire lifted risk sentiment, while lower oil prices and a weaker dollar on hopes of Hormuz flows supported the rand and equities.","backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-17T17:30:28Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-04-08T07:34:03Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-04-08T12:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"JA","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/stock-market-trading-screen-6531146.jpg","alt":"stock market trading screen (illustration)","credit":"sergeitokmakov","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/stock-market-trading-stocks-6531146/"}}